      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're looking for the grimy underbelly, so here are a few archetypes for your street-level characters. You've got the perpetually suspicious, low-level hustler who's always looking for a quick score, probably with a cheap, nervous energy. Then there's the silent enforcer, a hulking figure who doesn't speak much but whose presence is enough to keep people in line. Don't forget the corner informant, someone who knows everyone's secrets but only trades them for the smallest favor or dime. Finally, you need the washed-up local tough, a man clinging to a faded reputation from a better day, now just surviving on scraps and resentment.",
